      "value": "@{5e81599e846a8f679230d620|full_name}: Ah I see, I wasn't sure if you were using a laptop or PC, just a guess. So if you haven't had any problems in the past could it be some corrupt data you may have? If so, you could go onto steam and reinstall your files. All you'd need to do is right click on VRchat, go to properties, select the local files tab, then click on verify integrity of game files. That should take care of the issue. I'll be around to await your response.",
